{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1684","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Euclid Guess"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider Euclid's algorithm for finding the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", where $$$t$$$ is a list:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nfunction Euclid(a, b):\n    if a < b:\n        swap(a, b)\n\n    if b == 0:\n        return a\n\n    r = reminder from dividing a by b\n    if r > 0:\n        append r to the back of t\n\n    return Euclid(b, r)\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is an array $$$p$$$ of pairs of positive integers that are not greater than $$$m$$$. Initially, the list $$$t$$$ is empty. Then the function is run on each pair in $$$p$$$. After that the list $$$t$$$ is shuffled and given to you."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to find an array $$$p$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"of any size"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" not greater than $$$2 \\cdot 10^4$$$ that produces the given list $$$t$$$, or tell that no such array exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^3$$$, $$$1 \\le m \\le 10^9$$$) — the length of the array $$$t$$$ and the constraint for integers in pairs."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$t_1, t_2, \\ldots, t_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le t_i \\le m$$$) — the elements of the array $$$t$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the answer does not exist, output $$$-1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the answer exists, in the first line output $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le 2 \\cdot 10^4$$$) — the size of your array $$$p$$$, i. e. the number of pairs in the answer. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The $$$i$$$-th of the next $$$k$$$ lines should contain two integers $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i, b_i \\le m$$$) — the $$$i$$$-th pair in $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple valid answers you can output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 20\n1 8 1 6 3 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n19 11\n15 9\n3 7\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 10\n7 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n-1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 15\n1 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n15 8\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1000000000\n845063470\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n-1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample let's consider the array $$$t$$$ for each pair: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(19,\\, 11)$$$: $$$t = [8, 3, 2, 1]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(15,\\, 9)$$$: $$$t = [6, 3]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(3,\\, 7)$$$: $$$t = [1]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So in total $$$t = [8, 3, 2, 1, 6, 3, 1]$$$, which is the same as the input $$$t$$$ (up to a permutation)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case it is impossible to find such array $$$p$$$ of pairs that all integers are not greater than $$$10$$$ and $$$t = [7, 1]$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case for the pair $$$(15,\\, 8)$$$ array $$$t$$$ will be $$$[7, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1684G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1684/problem/G"}